--- !u!114 &4469658556881655090
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 3174281803529462771}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Virus enters the battlefield as a stealthy and adaptive enemy that cannot
    survive on its own but becomes dangerous once it invades living cells. It spreads
    quickly across lanes, hijacking healthy structures and forcing them to produce
    more copies of itself. Unlike ordinary bacteria, Virus relies on infiltration
    rather than brute strength, making it a fast and unpredictable attacker that
    pressures the player\u2019s defenses.\r\n\r\nVirus functions as a wave-based
    invader whose strength increases when left unchecked. It moves silently at first,
    then suddenly multiplies, overwhelming protective units if not countered in time.
    Some strains may resist basic treatments, forcing players to deploy the correct
    antiviral or supportive medicine units to stop replication and prevent further
    spread.\r\n\r\nVirus teaches players the importance of strategic protection rather
    than direct confrontation. Defensive medicines act as shields and targeted responses,
    blocking entry and suppressing replication before it spirals out of control.
    When the right medical defenders are placed wisely, Virus loses its advantage
    and the battlefield gradually returns to balance.\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3914de223fa8efc4787902589e5d6968, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 4947494457033249829, guid: 3914de223fa8efc4787902589e5d6968, type: 2}
