  m_text: Virus is a microscopic infectious agent that cannot carry out life processes
    on its own and must invade a living cell to survive and reproduce. It consists
    of genetic material, either DNA or RNA, enclosed in a protein coat, and sometimes
    surrounded by a lipid envelope, allowing it to attach to host cells and hijack
    their internal machinery.
